**`cig run` can use the VM too** (`cig run --engine vm`, `CIG_ENGINE=vm`, or `cig config engine vm`): a script is lowered to bytecode once and its module kept in the tin. Measured on another machine with this change's own build, so cig against itself only ([the run](docs/ENGINES-2026-11-22.md)): with its module in the tin the VM takes {{geomean.compute.cig-vm.cig-tree}} of the tree-walker's time over the {{n.compute.cig-vm.cig-tree}} compute programs, faster on {{faster.compute.cig-vm.cig-tree}}, level on {{level.compute.cig-vm.cig-tree}} and slower on {{slower.compute.cig-vm.cig-tree}}.
